{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3789","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3789","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3789\",\"parent_revision\":\"915107b206fea9cbfaef05555d5b5a48ba9c469b454b0330531dbfc586eb05cc\",\"root_revision\":\"915107b206fea9cbfaef05555d5b5a48ba9c469b454b0330531dbfc586eb05cc\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Impact\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nPlugin authors packaging a container-distributed MCP server get no guidance from the skill that is meant to cover MCP configuration. Two specific framing hazards are undocumented: whether the container invocation belongs in `command` + `args`, and how volume mounting affects server-side state across container recreation.\\n</div>\\n\\n## What Is Missing\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n`plugins/plugin-creator/skills/mcp-integration/` documents four MCP server types (stdio, SSE, HTTP, WebSocket), but no example covers a server distributed as a container image. A plugin author bundling a container-distributed MCP server has no documented configuration pattern for either of its two shapes: stdio over `docker run -i`, or an HTTP entry pointing at a separately started local container.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Where It Was Observed\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nEvery stdio example in the skill assumes a local executable or an npx-launched npm package:\\n\\n- `references/server-types-and-patterns.md:12` \u2014 `\\\"command\\\": \\\"npx\\\"` with `args: [\\\"-y\\\", \\\"@modelcontextprotocol/server-filesystem\\\", \\\"/allowed/path\\\"]`\\n- `SKILL.md` \\\"Dedicated .mcp.json\\\" example \u2014 `\\\"command\\\": \\\"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/servers/db-server\\\"`\\n\\nThat file's stdio section states \\\"Best for: file system access, local database connections, custom MCP servers, NPM-packaged servers\\\". Container distribution is absent from that list and from the skill directory.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Evidence\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n```\\ngit grep -in \\\"docker\\\\|container\\\" -- plugins/plugin-creator/skills/mcp-integration/\\n\u2192 0 matches\\n\\ngit grep -in \\\"docker\\\\|container\\\\|npx\\\" -- plugins/plugin-creator/skills/mcp-integration/\\n\u2192 1 match: references/server-types-and-patterns.md:12  \\\"command\\\": \\\"npx\\\"\\n```\\n\\nThe single match is the npm-package stdio example, not a container one.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Source\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nSurfaced by `research-insight-extractor` while processing `research/mcp-ecosystem/wigolo.md` (PR #3788). Confidence: High. Impact: Medium.\\n\\nwigolo is a concrete instance of the undocumented shape \u2014 it ships `ghcr.io/knockoutez/wigolo` and documents both a stdio and an HTTP container invocation \u2014 but the gap is in the skill, independent of that entry.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Note On Original Capture\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nThis item was captured by `backlog_add` into the local cache under reference `p1-mcp-integration-skill-documents-no-configuration-pattern-for`, but GitHub issue creation failed at the time with `403 GitHub GraphQL is not available from Claude Code sessions`, leaving `item_ref` empty. This issue is that capture, written through the GitHub MCP instead.\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"7cfc6591509e4326f8c2511113c5a2a1ec63a2a9765376c5a101b3e8cb5b2f28\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABXCEnsg\"}"}